                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "createdOn": 1710188823,
            "author": {
                "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                "username": "jagpalgill"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "How does one use this when the image is a collection of images (like PLDM) with the force update being set on a subset of components? I wonder if this should be in a PDI at the next (version/component?) level?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> How does one use this when the image is a collection of images (like PLDM) with the force update being set on a subset of components? \n\nRedfish has only support for singleton force update. Now why that is so its a question for DMTF Redfish.\n\n> I wonder if this should be in a PDI at the next (version/component?) level?\n\nThis is the property of StartUpdate DBus interface (not the version) which initiates the update . Version interface gets created as effect of StartUpdate flow."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "What if you don't support this property? How does bmcweb know to tell the user this isn't supported?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> What if you don't support this property? \n\nThats a good question, i think we should extend the Update interface to show this property if this is allowed, just like AllowedApplyTimes https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml?r=921791c73008a3edfc6507afb5bc15e48963d295#33.\nWill add that support.\n\n> How does bmcweb know to tell the user this isn't supported?\n\nAs per my understanding, I don't see there is an explicit way in current schema to show if Redfish UpdateService supports it or not. In all the flows this is being shown as property for update args or properties via \"ForceUpdate\" to be passed in for update operation.\nSo, i suppose this is something which needs to be requested from Redfish DMTF."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 24,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "> > What if you don't support this property? \n> \n> Thats a good question, i think we should extend the Update interface to show this property if this is allowed, just like AllowedApplyTimes https://grok.openbmc.org/xref/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Software/Update.interface.yaml?r=921791c73008a3edfc6507afb5bc15e48963d295#33.\n> Will add that support.\n\nUpdated the patch with the change.\n\n> \n> > How does bmcweb know to tell the user this isn't supported?\n> \n> As per my understanding, I don't see there is an explicit way in current schema to show if Redfish UpdateService supports it or not. In all the flows this is being shown as property for update args or properties via \"ForceUpdate\" to be passed in for update operation.\n> So, i suppose this is something which needs to be requested from Redfish DMTF.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions on above reasoning otherwise i will mark this comment as resolved. Thanks."
                }
            ],
